    "result": "All tests are now passing! Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n### 1. **Missing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` export** (governance.test.js)\nThe test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from the governance module, but it was only available in the default export. I added named exports for all schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) to `/packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`.\n\n### 2. **Toxicity metric parameter mismatch** (eval/index.test.js)  \nThe `toxicityMetric` function expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. When references were passed as the `bannedTerms` parameter, the function incorrectly flagged outputs that happened to contain strings from the references. I updated the signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references = [], bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` so it properly accepts both parameters and uses the default banned terms.\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests pass across 8 test files \u2713",
